The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ sum is greater than or equal to x and y" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(sum >= x && sum >= y);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If the return value is true, new list's last index of x is >= old list's last index of x" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, old list contains x and new list contains the same x" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == true && New_arrListContainsX == true && New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, old list's index of x is equal to new list's index of x" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, old list's last index of x is equal to new list's last index of x" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, old list's contains x is equal to new list's contains x" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == New_arrListContainsX);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ In all cases, the count of the new list should be greater than or equal to the count of the old list" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount >= Old_arrListCount);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, old list's count of elements is equal to new list's count of elements" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If the return value is not -1, the new list contains the old value" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX != -1);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, the return value of Old_arrList.Remove(x) is correctly calculated" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount + 1);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, the return value of Old_arrList.Insert(index, x) is correctly calculated" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount - 1);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, the index of x in the new list should be less than the index in the old list" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX < Old_arrListIndexOfX || New_arrListIndexOfX == 0);
</code>

The assert statement corresponding to the comment "@@@ If true, the last index of x in the new list should be greater than or equal the last index in the old list" is:
<code>
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
</code>
